{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Compute exact and sampled Shapley feature attributions to explain predictions of any machine learning model.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Game-Theoretic Interpretability with Kernel SHAP","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftExplain"}]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP"],"title":"SHAP Explainer APIs","anchor":"SHAP-Explainer-APIs"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations)"}]},{"text":" is a game-theoretic approach to explain the output of any machine learning model. It connects optimal credit allocation with local explanations using the classic Shapley values from cooperative game theory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"1. The Four Shapley Axioms","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"1-The-Four-Shapley-Axioms"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shapley values are the only attribution method that uniquely satisfies all four fundamental properties:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Efficiency"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Feature attributions sum up to the difference between model prediction ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f(x)"},{"type":"text","text":" and expected background prediction "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"E[f(X)]"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Σ_i=1..M φ_i = f(x) - E[f(X)]","type":"codeVoice"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Symmetry"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": If two features contribute equally to all possible feature subsets, their attributions are equal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dummy (Null Player)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": A feature that does not change the model prediction for any coalition receives an attribution of zero ("},{"code":"φ_i = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Additivity","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": For ensemble models "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f = f1 + f2"},{"type":"text","text":", attributions satisfy "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"φ_i(f) = φ_i(f1) + φ_i(f2)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"text":"2. Explaining Predictions in SwiftSci","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Explaining-Predictions-in-SwiftSci"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftExplain","import SwiftML","","\/\/ Initialize KernelSHAP with background dataset","let explainer = try KernelSHAP(","    model: { features in","        \/\/ Arbitrary inference closure","        return try await rf.predictProba(features: features).map { $0[1] }","    },","    background: backgroundSamples,","    nSamples: 100",")","","\/\/ Compute Shapley values for an instance","let instance = [35.0, 75000.0, 720.0, 1.0]","let explanation = try await explainer.explain(instance: instance)","","print(\"Base Value: \\(explanation.baseValue)\")","print(\"Feature Attributions: \\(explanation.values)\")"]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshaptheory"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAPTheory","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain","title":"SwiftExplain","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model Explainability, SHAP & Feature Attributions."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/KernelSHAP":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model interpretation using the KernelSHAP algorithm."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KernelSHAP","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KernelSHAP","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshap","title":"KernelSHAP","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP"}}}